Subject: [PATCH 23/25] Install the two evidenced Round-3 fixes (11.23 natva,
 11.43 agama), after catching a shared bug in both Gemini's and ChatGPT's
 proposed patches

Both external models answered the three GEMINI_CHATGPT_TASK_PROMPT_V3.md
tasks. Per this project's standing discipline, every claim was checked
against the actual running code before installing anything -- which
caught a real bug neither model's own "I tested this" claim caught.

Task A (sutra 11.23, natva-restoration-on-retake): both models agreed a
general tag-free ratva-at-a-distance engine is unsafe without
morphological tagging this project doesn't have; ChatGPT additionally
caught a real flaw in Gemini's first, more general proposal (it licensed
intervener consonants Panini 8.4.2 doesn't actually name), confirmed
independently against 8.4.2's own gloss. Installed only the one
evidenced case ("pra NaH" vs "na indraH") as a narrow, closed check
(NATVA_BOUNDARY_UPASARGAS_SLP1 = {"pra"}) in sanskrit_phonology.py.

Task B (sutra 11.43, shauddhakshara-agama): both models' proposed
4-entry lexical tables shared the same bug -- "DUfzadam" for
dhuuHsadam's Samhita form uses SLP1 "f" (the vocalic-r VOWEL) instead of
"r" (the repha CONSONANT), which decodes to a different, wrong word
("dhuu-r-imagined-as-vowel-Sadam"). Caught by actually running
slp1_to_deva() on it, not by trusting either model's claim of having
verified it. Fixed to "DUrzadam" before installing
SHAUDDHAKSHARA_AGAMA_SLP1. Restoration on Parigraha retake is automatic
by construction (verified against the real code path, not asserted) --
no separate restore function needed.

Found and fixed one more, unrelated, real bug along the way while
verifying this: pratishakhya_classify.REPHI_CACHE_SLP1 had two entries
("dhUHsadam", "durdhyaH") using invalid SLP1 (lowercase "dh" where a
single capital "D" is needed) that silently made is_rephi() always
return False for the words they were meant to cache. Fixed (encoding
only, not a change to which word each entry represents).

Task C (sutra 10.10-11's scope): both models say leave the existing
sutra-10.3 exception mechanism alone, matching this session's own
independent reasoning before the prompt was sent -- recorded as
"reasonably decided", not "proven"; no code change.

validate_krama_rv1_1.py's Test A-H suite is now 8/8 PASS, rescoped
honestly to the evidenced sub-cases (a general natva-at-a-distance or
Suddhaksara-derivation engine remains explicitly open, not claimed
solved). New tests in tests/test_krama_engine.py
(NatvaBoundaryAndShuddhaksharaAgama). Confirmed RV 1.1's own
regenerated output is byte-for-byte unchanged -- this is net-new
coverage, not a change to already-checked output.

Full detail in dge/RV_PRATISHAKHYA_KRAMA_ARCHITECTURE.md sec.6.13.

